[{:db/id -1, :doc/id "doc-90-docs-business-cloud-itonami-vertical-maturity.md", :doc/title "cloud-itonami — vertical maturity (design vs implementation)", :doc/path "90-docs/business/cloud-itonami-vertical-maturity.edn", :doc/body "# cloud-itonami — vertical maturity (design vs implementation)\n\n**As-of**: 2026-07-18  \n**Product**: `cloud-itonami`  \n**正本 (structured)**: `cloud-itonami-vertical-maturity.edn`  \n**Portfolio scores**: `maturity-facts.edn` + generated `maturity-scores.md` (ADR-2607021700)  \n**Flagship sprint**: ADR-2607122300  \n\nThis is the *within-product* breakdown. Portfolio BMC/YC answers “is the\nbusiness mature?”; this doc answers “where inside the fleet is that maturity?”\n\n## Rubric (0–5)\n\n| Axis | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **Design** | Domain scope, Governor discipline, op contract, ADR/blueprint clarity |\n| **Impl-core** | `operation` / governor|policy / `store` / `phase` / `sim` / `facts` present and tested |\n| **Impl-product** | Live demo, operator-quickstart, CI regen, pricing docs |\n| **Business** | External tenant, billing, hyp validation |\n\n## Fleet snapshot (mechanical)\n\nLocal ISIC checkouts under `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-*` (**n=165**):\n\n| module-score (0–6) | count | reading |\n|---|---:|---|\n| 6 | **127** | full actor modules |\n| 5 | 3 | near-full |\n| 0 | **35** | thin / empty src |\n\n| product-score (0–5) | count | reading |\n|---|---:|---|\n| 5 | **2** | 6399, 6310 only |\n| 4 | **1** | 7810 |\n| 3 | 16 | mostly mfg demos / sample HTML |\n| 1–2 | **146** | actor without storefront |\n\n`kotoba-lang/industry` registry (updated **2026-07-14T19:00:00Z**):\n\n| maturity | count |\n|---|---:|\n| `:implemented` | **286** |\n| `:blueprint` | 1 |\n| `:spec` | **345** |\n\n## Cohort table\n\n| Vertical / layer | Design | Impl-core | Impl-product | Business | One-liner |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|\n| **6399 Meta job-search** | 5 | 5 | 5 | **2** | Indeed replacement; 6 jurisdictions; live demo; aozora.app actor + first promo post (ADR-2607161930); Stripe Payment Link live for Managed Starter tier (ADR-2607161745), no paid org yet |\n| **6310 Talent** | 5 | 5 | 5 | **2** | kaonavi replacement; assignment op; live demo; aozora.app actor + first promo post (ADR-2607161930); Stripe Payment Link live for Managed Starter tier (ADR-2607161745), no paid org yet |\n| **7810 Employment/placement** | 4 | 4 | 4 | **2** | Near-flagship (demo + quickstart); Stripe Payment Link live for Managed Starter tier (ADR-2607161745), no paid org yet |\n| **Insurance / finance** | 4 | 4 | 1 | 0 | Full modules; almost no storefront |\n| **Real estate** | 4 | 4 | 1 | 0 | Same pattern |\n| **Health / care / hospital** | 5 | 4 | 1 | 0 | Strong clinical scope exclusion; thin product face |\n| **Education** | 4 | 4 | 1 | 0 | Full modules; no product face |\n| **Mfg / auto** | 4 | 4 | 3 | 0 | Higher demo-HTML rate; no operator funnel |\n| **2910 Motor-vehicle manufacture (next-up candidate)** | 4 | 4 | 3 | 0 | ISIC Rev.5 2910; full module set (operation/governor/store/phase/sim/facts) + robotics wired to a real physics/scene engine (ADR-2607151600). 2026-07-18 wave5 iteration 4: added `automotive.render-html` + `.github/workflows/regenerate.yml` -- `docs/samples/operator-console.html` (the file actually self-labeled 'Demo snapshot ... clojure -M:dev:run', NOT `docs/index.html` as ledger seq 3 misstated) is now build-time-generated through the real actor; verified idempotent locally, against a from-scratch CI-layout simulation, and via a live `workflow_dispatch` run (conclusion=success, https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-2910/actions/runs/29649931361, its own 'commit when changed' step logging 'console unchanged' confirming the byte-identical idempotent regeneration), and confirmed the live Pages URL now serves the generated content. Iteration 4 also found ledger seq 3's 'no operator-quickstart.md, no pricing/billing docs found' claim was incorrect -- both `docs/operator-quickstart.md` (52 lines) and `docs/business-model.md` (38 lines) already existed pre-iteration-4; `business-model.md` has qualitative revenue categories but no quantified pricing or Stripe link yet (checklist items 5/7 remain open). `docs/index.html` itself remains a static marketing page (not build-time-generated, but also not mislabeled as live data -- its own footer already says 'no invented usage or revenue metrics'). Still NOT promoted to the flagship cohort -- promotion is a separate decision this iteration did not make. |\n| **Infra / utility** | 4 | 3 | 1 | 0 | Some thinner checkouts |\n| **5820 CRM (Salesforce replace)** | 5 | 4 | 4 | **2** | RevOps-LLM ⊣ SubscriptionGovernor; live face /isic-5820/; kotoba-lang/crm west-registered (ADR-2607172500); pricing-intel 20260717-01 (¥50k–150k band); Stripe Payment Link live for Managed CRM Starter ¥80k/月 (ADR-2607172600), no paid org yet. ⚠ 2026-07-18 gap audit (ADR-2607189300 ledger seq 3): flagship checklist item 2 (build-time-generated demo) is NOT met -- docs/index.html was hand-authored in a single commit (cbbe532 'Lane C densify'), contains generic unfilled placeholders ('maturity unknown', literal `governor` name) and a broken CTA link to the wrong repo (isco-1212, not 5820); no generate.cljs/web/ build script exists anywhere in the repo history. Axis scores above are NOT re-verified against this finding -- flagged for human review, not auto-demoted per rollout guardrail. |\n| **Software/IT 620x** | 4 | 4 | 1 | 0 | 6201/6202/6209 CRM-fleet siblings sharing kotoba-lang/crm commons; thin product face |\n| **ISO3166 countries** | 4 | 4 | 1 | 0 | Country coordinators; no GTM surface |\n| **ISO3166 JPN agencies** | 4 | 0 | 1 | 0 | blueprint + docs; essentially no src |\n| **ISCO occupations** | 4 | 4 | 1 | 0 | open-occupation 88/88 :implemented (PR #427); product face still thin |\n| **Catalog / org surface** | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | github.io from registry SSoT |\n| **itonami.cloud cockpit** | 4 | 4 | 5 | 2 | free-path productSurface 5716/5716; free tenants=4; agentRuns7d~22k; Stripe readyForLiveCheckout (live); hyp/itonami-smb-pay measuring; no paid org yet |\n\n## Reading\n\n```\nDesign        ████████████████████  high across the factory\nImpl-core     ████████████████░░░░  ~77% of local ISIC full modules\nImpl-product  ██████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  cockpit + flagships; thin elsewhere\nBusiness      ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  free-tenant ok; paid hyp untested\n```\n\n**Design maturity and implementation maturity are not uncorrelated —\nimplementation has split into core vs product.** Core was mass-produced;\nproduct was invested in flagships + the itonami.cloud cockpit (now\nproductSurface 7/7); business has not cleared a paid gate on any vertical.\n\n## Priorities (from this table)\n\n1. ~~Owner STRIPE_*** secrets → live `/isco-1212` checkout~~ — **done\n   2026-07-16 (ADR-2607161620)**: secrets wired to Cloudflare Pages, live\n   Stripe Product/2 metered Price/Webhook created. Remaining gate is now\n   **E2E checkout verification (skipped, still open) → first paid org**.\n2. Prefer **product → business** on 6399 / 6310 (+7810) over new verticals. **5820 (Salesforce-replace CRM) joined this flagship cohort 2026-07-17** (owner directive; ADR-2607172600). 2026-07-18 audit found 5820's demo page is hand-authored, not build-time-generated (checklist item 2 gap, see cohort-table note; ADR-2607189300 ledger seq 3) -- still open, out of scope for a single bounded iteration (5820's actor shape has no HTML-render entrypoint at all). **isic-2910 (motor-vehicle manufacture) registered 2026-07-18 as the next-up new-vertical candidate** (same ADR, ledger seq 3); **its matching build-time-generation gap was closed 2026-07-18 wave5 iteration 4** (ledger seq 4, see cohort-table note) -- still not promoted to the flagship cohort.\n3. Keep the portfolio wedge narrative on the flagship pair (`:wedge 3` in\n   maturity-facts; not “all industries” as the sales wedge).\n4. Treat ISO3166 agencies and ISCO as **design assets**; defer runtime spend.\n5. Portfolio `validation` / `revenue` stay 0 until\n   `:hyp/itonami-smb-pay` (10 external paid orgs).\n6. **2026-07-18 wave5 iteration 5**: built a read-only fleet-wide diagnostic scanner\n   (`90-docs/business/scripts/flagship-checklist-scan.cljs`) instead of continuing\n   one-repo-at-a-time hand-diagnosis, and ran it over all 1,109 real local\n   `orgs/cloud-itonami-*` checkouts (1,116 dirs found, 7 without `.git`). Validated\n   against the 5 known-ground-truth repos before trusting it (isic-6399 correctly\n   scored fully clean; isic-5820 correctly scored no-generator; isic-6310/7810/2910\n   correctly flagged `checkout-lag=true`, explaining why their on-disk state still\n   looks unfixed even though iterations 1/2/4 already fixed them on GitHub — see\n   ledger seq 5 for the root cause, a `manifest/west.yml` pin-staleness bug this\n   iteration also fixed). **Strategic finding, reported instead of forcing a token\n   fix**: zero *new* \"cheap win\" repos exist (a repo with an existing generator\n   script but a missing nightly workflow) — the only 3 repos with any generator\n   script at all are the 3 already known. 930/1,109 (84%) of the fleet has **no\n   demo file whatsoever** (not even a hand-authored one); another 176/1,109 (16%)\n   have a hand-authored demo but no generator. The iteration-1/2 \"port the\n   isic-6399 regenerate.yml template\" playbook has run out of targets — closing\n   checklist item 2 on any new repo now requires a bespoke build-time renderer\n   written from that repo's own actor shape (the isic-2910 pattern, ledger seq 4),\n   roughly one iteration of work per repo, not a template port.\n\n## Related\n\n- Portfolio rescore note: `maturity-facts.edn` `:cloud-itonami` (2026-07-16)\n- Stripe billing go-live: ADR-2607161620\n- 6399/6310 aozora.app distribution actors: ADR-2607161930\n- 6399/6310/7810 flagship Managed-tier Stripe Payment Links + pricing-intelligence: ADR-2607161745\n- 5820 Salesforce-replace flagship promotion: ADR-2607172600\n- 5820 demo-generation gap audit + 2910 next-up candidate registration: ADR-2607189300 ledger seq 3 (2026-07-18)\n- 2910 build-time-demo-generation gap closed (automotive.render-html + regenerate.yml): ADR-2607189300 ledger seq 4 (2026-07-18)\n- Fleet-wide read-only diagnostic scanner + report: `90-docs/business/scripts/flagship-checklist-scan.cljs` / `90-docs/business/cloud-itonami-flagship-checklist-scan.edn` (generated), west.yml pin-staleness fix (commit f2c635cc): ADR-2607189300 ledger seq 5 (2026-07-18)\n- Metrics: `metrics/cloud-itonami.edn` (cockpit traffic)\n- Flagship depth: ADR-2607122300\n- Pattern saturation (earlier): ADR-2607011200", :doc/source-format "edn", :doc/doc_type "doc"}]